; SPDX-License-Identifier: 0BSD
; seiyaku.source.vla - Seiyaku (制約, "constraints"), a number-placement puzzle at rate zero
; (CART.14): eighty-one variables, twenty-seven constraints, one solution. The pass expands
; this file into seiyaku.vla beside it, the rows the engine loads (docs/SPEC.md section 7.8):
; edit this one, then expand it again with
;   cargo run --release --example expand
; Its book, the block near its end, is written by
;   cargo run --release --example seiyaku
; and never by hand.
;
; How to play. The Board is nine rows of nine variables, in nine boxes of three by three.
; Each row, each column and each box is a constraint: it holds each value from 1 to 9 once.
; The instance fixes some values, its givens, drawn in black, and a value you assign is drawn
; in lavender. Move with the arrows, Page Up
; and Page Down, Home and End, and the mouse; then, as the keys beside the Board say too:
;   1 to 9, on the row of digits or the keypad: assign the value to the variable the
;     selection stands on.
;   Backspace: retract the assignment; on an unassigned variable, strike every mark.
;   Q W E, A S D, Z X C: mark a value in the variable's domain, or strike it, each key where
;     its mark stands in the cell: Q the 1 at the top left, S the 5 in the middle, C the 9.
;   F: fill every unassigned variable's domain with the values its constraints still allow.
;   R: retract every assignment and strike every mark.
;   N: a new instance. G: the next instance's grade, 1 to 4 and round.
;   I: infer. The next inference the three techniques make is said under the Board; pressed
;     again, it is applied and the next one said, so that I, again and again, walks the puzzle.
;   P: propagate. Inference after inference is applied until none is left, and the words say
;     where it stopped: satisfied, a contradiction, or as far as the three techniques reach.
;   U: retract every assignment inference made, and leave yours.
;   M: draw only the marks the constraints still allow, the rest kept beneath; again, all.
; A variable whose value repeats in one of its constraints is violated, and drawn red. When
; every variable is assigned and no constraint is violated, the instance is satisfied, and
; the Board turns Lovelace Lavender, its digits white. While I or P has lit the words, the
; Board lights the inference they say: a single's variable in Lovelace Lavender, its value
; drawn white before it is applied, or the places a pointing strikes its value from; what it
; is read by on a pale lavender; and a domain with no value left as ∅ on the red. The
; Constraints sheet keeps the counts and each constraint's state. Clock!B3 is the seed:
; everyone who types the same seed is dealt the same instances.
;
; The words are constraint programming's: a cell is a variable, a digit a value, an entry an
; assignment, an erasure a retraction, the pencil marks the variable's domain, a conflict a
; violated constraint, solved satisfied, and a puzzle an instance.
;
; Where the instances come from (CART.14, decisions 7 to 9). The book holds 128 puzzles, 32 a
; grade, each with one solution, written by the generator of engine/src/seiyaku.rs, which
; cargo test holds by two solvers. A grade is the hardest technique a puzzle needs: 1 naked
; singles, 2 hidden singles, 3 pointing pairs, 4 beyond the three. An instance is its puzzle
; transformed by the seed and the instance's number: the bands permuted and the rows within
; each band, the stacks and the columns within each stack, a transposition, and the values
; relabeled. Each is a symmetry of the rules, so the instance keeps its puzzle's one solution
; and its grade.
;
; How it settles. The cartridge says (settle 165): after an act the engine steps the board
; again, with no act, until a frame changes nothing (docs/SPEC.md section 5, version 6). An
; act is three frames, its own, the one after the engine releases its command, and one that
; proves nothing moved; the load settles too, so the board opens on its values. Propagation
; is an inference a frame across the settle's steps (CART.14.1, decisions 4 and 14): at most
; 81 assignments and 81 strikes, since a box and a value point once until a person acts
; again, and the frames around them.
;
; How it infers (CART.14.1's second slice). Every frame the Ladder sheet names the next
; inference from the candidates, the values the constraints still allow less those struck,
; in the grader's order (engine/src/seiyaku.rs, grade): a naked single, a variable with one
; value left; a hidden single, a value with one place left in a row, a column or a box; and
; a pointing pair or triple, a box whose places for a value all lie on one line, the value
; struck from the rest of that line. A frame applies what the last one named, through the
; person's own path, the Lab's assignment and place, or the Struck sheet, so no cell reads
; itself. The ladder reads the constraints alone and never the person's marks.
;
; What a rule costs (docs/SPEC.md section 2), and how this source keeps it:
;   - The constraints are counted by COUNTIF over the Grid: a unit's count of a value is one
;     COUNTIF over its row, column or box, a fill a table, read by the unit's nine variables
;     through INDEX.
;   - A command is read once, in a cell of the Lab, and every variable reads that cell.
;   - The marks' text is built by & and never compared, a mark read by BITAND.
;   - The ladder counts each unit's places for each value by SUM over the candidates' planes,
;     a flip reaching only its own value's counts (CART.14.1, decision 8), and finds the
;     first of each technique by MIN over keys that sort as the grader's order does.

(cartridge "seiyaku"
  (spec 6)                          ; the version of docs/SPEC.md this cartridge is written to: an act's place, (settle K), (bound ...), (game ...) and (read ...)
  (title "Seiyaku 制約")            ; what the host shows: the name and its kanji, "constraints"
  (rate 0)                          ; an act steps the board; nothing else does
  (screen grid 9 9)                 ; the Screen, hidden: the Camera shows the Board in its place
  (seed host)                       ; the host's seed, new instances each load; a seed typed into Clock!B3 brings them back
  (settle 165)                      ; an act's settle, at most 165 steps: propagation's assignments and strikes, and the frames around them
  (bound "Board")                   ; the Board drawn to its extent and no further
  (game "Board" "Constraints")      ; the game's keys on both tabs, G where the next grade shows among them
  (read "Board" "Constraints")      ; read-only: no key or row of a person's writes either, so no cell loses its formula
  (author "Spreadsheet Company")    ; who wrote it
  (license "0BSD")                  ; the header's twin: copy this file to start a game of your own
  (notes "Seiyaku 制約: eighty-one variables, twenty-seven constraints, one solution, proven before you began. 1 to 9, the row's or the keypad's, assign a value to the variable the selection stands on and Backspace retracts it; Q W E, A S D and Z X C mark a value in its domain, each key where its mark stands in the cell; F fills every unassigned domain with the values its constraints allow; R retracts every assignment, N deals a new instance and G sets the next instance's grade. I says the next inference and, again, applies it; P propagates to the fixed point; U retracts what inference assigned; M draws only the marks the constraints allow."))

; The library whose macros this source calls: sheets, labels and headers; cells, rules
; and on, each naming a sheet once over a run of its rows; rule and priority; count and first-frame;
; camera; and picture, which writes the book. Since KIT.5 every rule is written as
; expressions, which the formula syntax writes to the same bytes: a reference computed
; from a number is a ref into its sheet, or, on the rule's own sheet, a symbol fused from
; its letters and its row.
(include "../common.vla")

; ---- the sheets, in tab order ----------------------------------------------------------
; The Board and the Constraints a person sees; the rest hidden, each a layer of the rule.
(sheets "Board" "Constraints")
(sheet "Book" hidden)
(sheet "Deal" hidden)
(sheet "Givens" hidden)
(sheet "Entries" hidden)
(sheet "Marks" hidden)
(sheet "Grid" hidden)
(sheet "Units" hidden)
(sheet "Candidates" hidden)
(sheet "Violations" hidden)
(sheet "Struck" hidden)
(sheet "Across" hidden)
(sheet "Down" hidden)
(sheet "Boxes" hidden)
(sheet "Open" hidden)
(sheet "Naked" hidden)
(sheet "Hidden" hidden)
(sheet "Forced" hidden)
(sheet "Ladder" hidden)
(sheet "Inferred" hidden)
(sheet "Drawn" hidden)
(sheet "Light" hidden)
(sheet "Lab" hidden)
(sheet "Screen" hidden)
(sheet "Camera" hidden)
(sheet "Commands" hidden)

; ---- the Camera: the Board shown in the Screen's place (docs/SPEC.md section 3.8) --------
(camera 1 1)
(cells "Camera" ("A3" "sheet") ("B3" "Board"))

; ---- the commands (docs/SPEC.md section 3.10), each a key on the viewport at rate 0 ----
; Empty holds hold always. A command on a variable stands on the cell the selection stands
; on, and touches nothing on another sheet; domains, retract-all, instance and grade act
; from any sheet.
(headers "Commands" "A1" "name" "words" "holds" "key")
(cells "Commands"
  ("A2" "assign-1")    ("B2" "assign 1 to the variable the selection stands on, unless the instance fixes it")  ("D2" "Digit1")
  ("A3" "assign-2")    ("B3" "assign 2 to the variable the selection stands on, unless the instance fixes it")  ("D3" "Digit2")
  ("A4" "assign-3")    ("B4" "assign 3 to the variable the selection stands on, unless the instance fixes it")  ("D4" "Digit3")
  ("A5" "assign-4")    ("B5" "assign 4 to the variable the selection stands on, unless the instance fixes it")  ("D5" "Digit4")
  ("A6" "assign-5")    ("B6" "assign 5 to the variable the selection stands on, unless the instance fixes it")  ("D6" "Digit5")
  ("A7" "assign-6")    ("B7" "assign 6 to the variable the selection stands on, unless the instance fixes it")  ("D7" "Digit6")
  ("A8" "assign-7")    ("B8" "assign 7 to the variable the selection stands on, unless the instance fixes it")  ("D8" "Digit7")
  ("A9" "assign-8")    ("B9" "assign 8 to the variable the selection stands on, unless the instance fixes it")  ("D9" "Digit8")
  ("A10" "assign-9")   ("B10" "assign 9 to the variable the selection stands on, unless the instance fixes it") ("D10" "Digit9")
  ("A11" "retract")    ("B11" "retract the variable's assignment; on an unassigned variable, strike every mark") ("D11" "Backspace")
  ("A12" "domain-1")   ("B12" "mark 1 in the variable's domain, or strike it")                                   ("D12" "KeyQ")
  ("A13" "domain-2")   ("B13" "mark 2 in the variable's domain, or strike it")                                   ("D13" "KeyW")
  ("A14" "domain-3")   ("B14" "mark 3 in the variable's domain, or strike it")                                   ("D14" "KeyE")
  ("A15" "domain-4")   ("B15" "mark 4 in the variable's domain, or strike it")                                   ("D15" "KeyA")
  ("A16" "domain-5")   ("B16" "mark 5 in the variable's domain, or strike it")                                   ("D16" "KeyS")
  ("A17" "domain-6")   ("B17" "mark 6 in the variable's domain, or strike it")                                   ("D17" "KeyD")
  ("A18" "domain-7")   ("B18" "mark 7 in the variable's domain, or strike it")                                   ("D18" "KeyZ")
  ("A19" "domain-8")   ("B19" "mark 8 in the variable's domain, or strike it")                                   ("D19" "KeyX")
  ("A20" "domain-9")   ("B20" "mark 9 in the variable's domain, or strike it")                                   ("D20" "KeyC")
  ("A21" "domains")    ("B21" "fill every unassigned variable's domain with the values its constraints still allow") ("D21" "KeyF")
  ("A22" "retract-all") ("B22" "retract every assignment and strike every mark of the instance")                 ("D22" "KeyR")
  ("A23" "instance")   ("B23" "deal a new instance, at the next instance's grade")                               ("D23" "KeyN")
  ("A24" "grade")      ("B24" "the next instance's grade: 1, 2, 3, 4 and round")                                 ("D24" "KeyG")
  ("A25" "infer")      ("B25" "say the next inference; pressed again, apply it and say the next")                ("D25" "KeyI")
  ("A26" "propagate")  ("B26" "apply inference after inference to the fixed point, and say where it stopped")    ("D26" "KeyP")
  ("A27" "retract-inferred") ("B27" "retract every assignment inference made")                                   ("D27" "KeyU")
  ("A28" "filter")     ("B28" "draw only the marks the constraints still allow, or every mark again")            ("D28" "KeyM"))

; ---- the Lab: the counts, and the act read once ---------------------------------------
; The acts of this instance, the instances dealt, the restarts; the next instance's grade,
; 2 at the load, and this instance's; the act's value, its mark, a retraction, the domains
; filled, and the variable it stands on, 1 to 81 or 0; satisfied, and the acts it took. Then
; the ladder's (CART.14.1's second slice): its words lit, a propagation running, an inference
; applied at this frame, an assignment or a strike, the marks filtered; the person's own
; value and place, which the assigned and the place are unless an inference assigns; and the
; strikes cleared.
(labels "Lab" "A1" "acts" "instances" "restarts" "next grade" "grade" "assigned" "marked" "retract" "domains" "place" "satisfied" "satisfied in"
  "lit" "propagating" "applied" "assigns" "strikes" "filtered" "the person's value" "the person's place" "strikes cleared")

(defmacro (the-variables-filled)
  "how many variables hold a value, given or assigned"
  (countif Grid!A1:I9 ">0"))

(defmacro (a-command word)
  "the command named by the word, run at this frame: Input!$B$20=\"word\""
  (= Input!$B$20 word))

(defmacro (named-as prefix k)
  "a command's value when it is the prefix and k, assign-k or domain-k: (Input!$B$20=\"prefix-k\")*k"
  (* (a-command (&expand prefix k)) k))

(rules "Lab"
  ("B1" (if (or (<> Lab!B2 Lab.last!B2) (<> Lab!B3 Lab.last!B3)) 0 (+ Lab.last!B1 (if (or (= Input!$B$13 1) (= Input!$B$14 1) (= Input!$B$15 1) (<> Input!$B$20 "")) 1 0)))))
(count "Lab" "B2" (if (a-command "instance") 1 0))
(count "Lab" "B3" (if (a-command "retract-all") 1 0))
(first-frame "Lab" "B4" 2 (if (a-command "grade") (+ (mod Lab.last!B4 4) 1) Lab.last!B4))
(defmacro (the-ladder-asked)
  "infer or propagate run at this frame, which light the ladder's words"
  (or (a-command "infer") (a-command "propagate")))

(defmacro (an-inference-named)
  "the last frame's ladder named an inference: an assignment or a strike"
  (> Ladder.last!$B$1 0))

(defmacro (the-inference-applied)
  "the last frame's inference applied at this one: while a propagation runs, or at infer pressed while its words were lit"
  (and (an-inference-named)
       (or (= Lab!B14 1)
           (and (a-command "infer") (= Lab.last!B13 1)))))

(rules "Lab"
  ("B5" (if (or (= Clock!$B$1 1) (<> Lab!B2 Lab.last!B2)) Lab!B4 Lab.last!B5))
  ("B6" (if (= Lab!B16 1) Ladder.last!$B$2 Lab!B19))   ; the value assigned: the inference's, or the person's
  ("B7" (+ (each (k (1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9)) (named-as "domain-" k))))
  ("B8" (if (a-command "retract") 1 0))
  ("B9" (if (a-command "domains") 1 0))
  ("B10" (if (= Lab!B16 1) Ladder.last!$B$3 Lab!B20))  ; the place acted on: the inference's, or the person's
  ("B11" (if (and (= (the-variables-filled) 81) (= (sum Violations!A1:I9) 0)) 1 0))
  ("B12" (if (= Lab!B11 1) (if (= Lab.last!B11 1) Lab.last!B12 Lab!B1) 0))
  ("B13" (priority
           ((the-ladder-asked) 1)
           ((<> Input!$B$20 "") 0)                       ; any other command puts the words out
           (else Lab.last!B13)))
  ("B14" (priority
           ((a-command "propagate") 1)
           ((and (= Lab.last!B14 1) (an-inference-named)) 1)
           (else 0)))
  ("B15" (if (the-inference-applied) 1 0))
  ("B16" (if (and (= Lab!B15 1) (< Ladder.last!$B$1 3)) 1 0))   ; a naked or a hidden single assigns
  ("B17" (if (and (= Lab!B15 1) (= Ladder.last!$B$1 3)) 1 0))   ; a pointing strikes
  ("B19" (+ (each (k (1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9)) (named-as "assign-" k))))
  ("B20" (if (and (= Input!$B$19 "Board") (>= Input!$B$11 2) (<= Input!$B$11 10) (>= Input!$B$12 2) (<= Input!$B$12 10)) (+ (* (- Input!$B$12 2) 9) (- Input!$B$11 1)) 0)))
(first-frame "Lab" "B18" 0 (if (a-command "filter") (- 1 Lab.last!B18) Lab.last!B18))

; ---- the Deal: the instance's puzzle, and its transform --------------------------------
; Rows 10 to 44 hash the seed, the instance and the row: Life's soup hash, two linear forms
; modulo the prime multiplied, every product under 2^53. Each hash times 64 and its row is a
; key no other equals, and a key's rank among its group's, the keys below it counted, is a
; permutation: the values (rows 11 to 19), the bands (20 to 22), each band's rows (23 to 31),
; the stacks (32 to 34) and each stack's columns (35 to 43). Row 10 names the puzzle in its
; grade's block of the book and row 44 whether the instance is transposed. F1:F9 hold each
; row's source row and G1:G9 each column's source column.
(labels "Deal" "A1" "puzzle" "transposed")
(headers "Deal" "B9" "hash" "key" "rank")

(defmacro (the-third)
  "this row's third of the nine, 1 to 3, which names its band or its stack"
  (+ (int (/ (- (row) 1) 3)) 1))

(rules "Deal"
  ("B1" (+ (* 32 (- Lab!$B$5 1)) 1 (mod B10 32)))
  ("B2" (mod B44 2))
  ("F1:F9" (+ (* 3 (- (index $D$20:$D$22 (the-third)) 1)) D23))
  ("G1:G9" (+ (* 3 (- (index $D$32:$D$34 (the-third)) 1)) D35))
  ("B10:B44" (mod (* (mod (+ (* Clock!$B$3 1103515) (* Lab!$B$2 7919) (* (row) 1597334) 3440100) 67108859)
                   (mod (+ (* Clock!$B$3 2012345) (* Lab!$B$2 104729) (* (row) 1209487) 3213021) 67108859))
                67108859))
  ("C10:C44" (+ (* B10 64) (row)))
  ("D11:D19" (+ 1 (countif C$11:C$19 (& "<" C11)))))

(defmacro (ranks-of-three first)
  "the ranks of three keys among themselves, from the first's row: the bands, the stacks, a band's rows or a stack's columns"
  (rule "Deal" (&expand "D" first ":D" (+expand first 2))
    (+ 1 (countif (symbol "C$" first ":C$" (+expand first 2)) (& "<" (symbol "C" first))))))

(ranks-of-three 20)                 ; the bands
(ranks-of-three 23)                 ; the first band's rows
(ranks-of-three 26)                 ; the second band's rows
(ranks-of-three 29)                 ; the third band's rows
(ranks-of-three 32)                 ; the stacks
(ranks-of-three 35)                 ; the first stack's columns
(ranks-of-three 38)                 ; the second stack's columns
(ranks-of-three 41)                 ; the third stack's columns

; ---- the Givens: the puzzle transformed ------------------------------------------------
; A11:I19, each variable's value in the puzzle, read from the Book at the puzzle's row and at
; its source, the puzzle's row and column its own row's and column's sources, swapped when
; transposed; A1:I9, that value relabeled.
(defmacro (the-source)
  "the column of the Book this variable reads: its source row and source column as one place, swapped when transposed"
  (if (= Deal!$B$2 1)
    (+ (* (- (index Deal!$F$1:$F$9 (column)) 1) 9) Deal!$G1)
    (+ (* (- Deal!$F1 1) 9) (index Deal!$G$1:$G$9 (column)))))

(rules "Givens"
  ("A11:I19" (index Book!$A$1:$CC$128 Deal!$B$1 (the-source)))
  ("A1:I9" (if (= A11 0) 0 (index Deal!$D$11:$D$19 A11))))

; ---- the person's state: the assignments and the marks -----------------------------------
; Each variable a formula of its own last value and the act (CART.14, decision 2): a new
; instance or a restart empties it; a given is never assigned or marked; an act on it assigns
; a value, retracts, or marks a value, an assigned variable's marks kept and none changed;
; domains fills every unassigned variable's marks with its candidates, Candidates!A83:I91.
; A mark is a bit: the marks are one number, 1 for the 1, 2 for the 2, 256 for the 9.
(defmacro (a-new-instance)
  "a new instance or a restart this frame: the instances or the restarts counted moved"
  (or (<> Lab!$B$2 Lab.last!$B$2) (<> Lab!$B$3 Lab.last!$B$3)))

(defmacro (this-variable)
  "the variable this cell is, 1 to 81, as the Lab numbers the act's place"
  (+ (* (- (row) 1) 9) (column)))

(defmacro (the-mark)
  "the bit of the value the act marks: 2 to the value less one"
  (^ 2 (- Lab!$B$7 1)))

(defmacro (bit-of cell k)
  "a bit of a number of marks, 1 or 0: the number and k, 2 to the mark's place, by BITAND"
  (if (> (bitand cell k) 0) 1 0))

(defmacro (an-act-here)
  "true where the act stands on this variable"
  (= Lab!$B$10 (this-variable)))

(defmacro (the-assignment-acted-on)
  "an act on this variable: it assigns a value, or retracts, or leaves the assignment as it was"
  (priority
    ((> Lab!$B$6 0) Lab!$B$6)
    ((= Lab!$B$8 1) 0)
    (else Entries.last!A1)))

(defmacro (inferred-and-retracted)
  "retract-inferred run at this frame, on a variable inference assigned"
  (and (a-command "retract-inferred") (= Inferred.last!A1 1)))

(rule "Entries" "A1:I9"
  (priority
    ((a-new-instance) 0)                       ; a new instance or a restart empties it
    ((> Givens!A1 0) 0)                        ; a given is never assigned
    ((inferred-and-retracted) 0)               ; U takes back what inference assigned
    ((an-act-here) (the-assignment-acted-on))
    (else Entries.last!A1)))                   ; else as it was

; The variables inference assigned, each 1 until a retraction, a person's assignment over it,
; a restart or a new instance; the Constraints sheet counts them, and U retracts them.
(rule "Inferred" "A1:I9"
  (priority
    ((a-new-instance) 0)
    ((= Entries!A1 0) 0)                       ; retracted, or never assigned
    ((and (= Lab!$B$16 1) (an-act-here)) 1)    ; inference assigned it at this frame
    ((<> Entries!A1 Entries.last!A1) 0)        ; the person assigned over it
    (else Inferred.last!A1)))

; The strikes cleared (CART.14.1, decision 7): an assignment only narrows the domains, so the
; strikes hold across one; a retraction or an overwrite of any variable widens them, and a
; restart or a new instance begins again, so each clears every strike.
(defmacro (a-value-taken-back)
  "some variable assigned at the last frame holds another value or none at this one"
  (> (sumproduct (* (> Entries.last!A1:I9 0) (<> Entries!A1:I9 Entries.last!A1:I9))) 0))

(rule "Lab" "B21" (if (or (a-new-instance) (a-value-taken-back)) 1 0))

(defmacro (the-domain-filled)
  "domains: an unassigned variable's marks its candidates, an assigned variable's kept"
  (if (> Entries!A1 0) Marks.last!A1 Candidates!A83))

(defmacro (the-mark-toggled)
  "the act's value marked in the domain, or struck where it stands marked: its bit flipped"
  (bitxor Marks.last!A1 (the-mark)))

(defmacro (the-marks-acted-on)
  "an act on this variable: a mark on an unassigned variable toggled, a retraction of an unassigned variable striking every mark, or the marks as they were"
  (priority
    ((and (> Lab!$B$7 0) (= Entries!A1 0)) (the-mark-toggled))
    ((and (= Lab!$B$8 1) (= Entries.last!A1 0)) 0)
    (else Marks.last!A1)))

(rule "Marks" "A1:I9"
  (priority
    ((a-new-instance) 0)                       ; a new instance or a restart strikes every mark
    ((> Givens!A1 0) 0)                        ; a given is never marked
    ((= Lab!$B$9 1) (the-domain-filled))
    ((an-act-here) (the-marks-acted-on))
    (else Marks.last!A1)))                     ; else as it was

(rule "Marks" "A11:I19"
  (+ (each (k (1 2 4 8 16 32 64 128 256)) (bit-of A1 k))))
(rule "Grid" "A1:I9" (+ Givens!A1 Entries!A1))

; ---- the constraints counted (CART.14, decision 5; by COUNTIF since CART.14.1) --------------
; The Units: A1:I9 each row's count of each value, a row a row and a value a column;
; A11:I19 each column's, a value a row and a column a column; A21:I29 each box's, a box a row
; and a value a column. A fill a table, and a fill a box, since no fill moves a range by threes.
(rule "Units" "A1:I9" (countif Grid!$A1:$I1 (column)))
(rule "Units" "A11:I19" (countif Grid!A$1:A$9 (- (row) 10)))
(rule "Units" "A21:I21" (countif Grid!$A$1:$C$3 (column)))   ; box 1
(rule "Units" "A22:I22" (countif Grid!$D$1:$F$3 (column)))   ; box 2
(rule "Units" "A23:I23" (countif Grid!$G$1:$I$3 (column)))   ; box 3
(rule "Units" "A24:I24" (countif Grid!$A$4:$C$6 (column)))   ; box 4
(rule "Units" "A25:I25" (countif Grid!$D$4:$F$6 (column)))   ; box 5
(rule "Units" "A26:I26" (countif Grid!$G$4:$I$6 (column)))   ; box 6
(rule "Units" "A27:I27" (countif Grid!$A$7:$C$9 (column)))   ; box 7
(rule "Units" "A28:I28" (countif Grid!$D$7:$F$9 (column)))   ; box 8
(rule "Units" "A29:I29" (countif Grid!$G$7:$I$9 (column)))   ; box 9

; A variable is violated where its value counts twice in its row, its column or its box.
(defmacro (the-box-from top)
  "the variable's box, 1 to 9, where its nine rows of variables start at the row top"
  (+ (* 3 (int (/ (- (row) top) 3))) (int (/ (- (column) 1) 3)) 1))

(defmacro (its-row-count)
  "the variable's value counted in its row: the Units' row by its own, the value the column"
  (index Units!$A1:$I1 Grid!A1))

(defmacro (its-column-count)
  "the variable's value counted in its column: the Units' column by its own, the value the row"
  (index Units!A$11:A$19 Grid!A1))

(defmacro (its-box-count)
  "the variable's value counted in its box: the Units' boxes by its own, the value the column"
  (index Units!$A$21:$I$29 (the-box-from 1) Grid!A1))

(rule "Violations" "A1:I9"
  (if (= Grid!A1 0) 0
    (if (or (> (its-row-count) 1) (> (its-column-count) 1) (> (its-box-count) 1)) 1 0)))

; ---- the strikes: the values a pointing took out of a domain (CART.14.1, decision 7) -------
; Each variable's strikes a number of bits, as its marks are: a pointing the last frame named
; and this frame applies strikes its value from every unassigned variable on its line outside
; its box; the Lab's B21 clears them all.
(defmacro (on-the-line-outside-the-box down line box)
  "the variable lies on a pointing's line, its column where down is 1 and else its row, outside the pointing's box"
  (and (if (= down 1)
         (= (column) line)
         (= (row) line))
       (<> (the-box-from 1) box)))

(defmacro (on-the-struck-line)
  "the variable lies on the line the last frame's pointing named, outside its box"
  (on-the-line-outside-the-box Ladder.last!$B$6 Ladder.last!$B$7 Ladder.last!$B$5))

(defmacro (struck-here)
  "a strike applied at this frame to this unassigned variable"
  (and (= Lab!$B$17 1) (= Grid!A1 0) (on-the-struck-line)))

(rule "Struck" "A1:I9"
  (priority
    ((= Lab!$B$21 1) 0)                                                 ; cleared
    ((struck-here) (bitor Struck.last!A1 Ladder.last!$B$4))             ; the pointing's value struck
    (else Struck.last!A1)))

; A value is a candidate of an unassigned variable where it counts in none of its three
; constraints and no pointing struck it: nine planes, the value v's at rows 9 (v - 1) + 1 to
; 9 v, each a fill; A83:I91 the candidates as marks, which F fills a domain with.
(defmacro (candidate-plane bit letter top bottom units-row)
  "a plane of candidates from the row top to the row bottom: the value's bit not struck, and its counts in the Units' column letter, its columns' on units-row"
  (rule "Candidates" (&expand "A" top ":I" bottom)
    (if (and (= Grid!A1 0)
             (= (bitand Struck!A1 bit) 0)
             (= (ref "Units" (&expand "$" letter 1)) 0)
             (= (ref "Units" (&expand "A$" units-row)) 0)
             (= (index (ref "Units" (&expand "$" letter "$21:$" letter "$29")) (the-box-from top)) 0))
      1 0)))

(each-index (v bit (1 2 4 8 16 32 64 128 256) 1)
  (candidate-plane bit (column-letters-expand v) (+expand (*expand 9 (-expand v 1)) 1) (*expand 9 v) (+expand 10 v)))

(rule "Candidates" "A83:I91"
  (+ A1 (* 2 A10) (* 4 A19) (* 8 A28) (* 16 A37) (* 32 A46) (* 64 A55) (* 128 A64) (* 256 A73)))

; ---- the open places: each unit's count of each value's places left (decision 8) ----------
; Across, a row a row of the planes (9 (v - 1) + r): A to C the places in each stack's three
; columns, D the row's whole count. Down, a row a band of a plane (3 (v - 1) + band + 1): A to
; I the places in each column's three rows of the band. Boxes, Down's rows: A to C each
; stack's box. Open, laid out as the Units are: A1:I9 each row's places for each value, a value
; a column; A11:I19 each column's, a value a row; A21:I29 each box's, a value a column.
(rule "Across" "A1:A81" (sum Candidates!$A1:$C1))
(rule "Across" "B1:B81" (sum Candidates!$D1:$F1))
(rule "Across" "C1:C81" (sum Candidates!$G1:$I1))
(rule "Across" "D1:D81" (sum A1:C1))

(defmacro (a-band-down row top)
  "a row of Down: the value's places in each column within a band, its plane's three rows from top summed"
  (rule "Down" (&expand "A" row ":I" row)
    (sum (ref "Candidates" (&expand "A" top ":A" (+expand top 2))))))

(each (v (1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9))
  (each (band (0 1 2))
    (a-band-down
      (+expand (*expand 3 (-expand v 1)) (+expand band 1))
      (+expand (*expand 9 (-expand v 1)) (+expand (*expand 3 band) 1)))))

(rule "Boxes" "A1:A27" (sum Down!$A1:$C1))
(rule "Boxes" "B1:B27" (sum Down!$D1:$F1))
(rule "Boxes" "C1:C27" (sum Down!$G1:$I1))

(defmacro (a-value-across v row)
  "Open's column of the value v: each row's places left for it, the Across sheet's whole counts from its plane's first row"
  (rule "Open" (&expand (column-letters-expand v) "1:" (column-letters-expand v) "9")
    (ref "Across" (&expand "$D" row))))

(defmacro (a-value-down row top)
  "Open's row of a value among the columns: each column's places left for it, its three bands in Down from top summed"
  (rule "Open" (&expand "A" row ":I" row)
    (sum (ref "Down" (&expand "A" top ":A" (+expand top 2))))))

(each (v (1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9))
  (a-value-across v (+expand (*expand 9 (-expand v 1)) 1))
  (a-value-down (+expand 10 v) (+expand (*expand 3 (-expand v 1)) 1)))

(defmacro (the-band-of-the-box top)
  "a box's band, 0 to 2, where the rows of the boxes start at top"
  (int (/ (- (row) top) 3)))

(defmacro (the-stack-of-the-box top)
  "a box's stack, 0 to 2, where the rows of the boxes start at top"
  (mod (- (row) top) 3))

(rule "Open" "A21:I29"
  (index Boxes!$A$1:$C$27
    (+ (* 3 (- (column) 1)) (the-band-of-the-box 21) 1)
    (+ (the-stack-of-the-box 21) 1)))

; ---- the three techniques' keys: each one's first by MIN, in the grader's order (decision 9) ----
; Naked: a variable with one value left, 10 times the variable and the value. Hidden: each
; unit's first value with one place left, 100 times the unit and the value, the rows units 1
; to 9 (A1:A9), the columns 10 to 18 (A11:I11) and the boxes 19 to 27 (A21:A29); the place,
; Forced, the variable in that unit holding that value. A pointing, Across!E1:G81 by rows and
; Down!A31:I57 by columns: a box's two or more places for a value all on one line, the line
; holding more beyond the box, 10000 times the box, 100 times the value, 10 for a column and
; the line. 9999 and 999999 are none.
(defmacro (none-naked) 9999)

(defmacro (none-pointing) 999999)

(rule "Naked" "A1:I9"
  (iferror
    (+ (* 10 (this-variable)) (match Candidates!A83 (quote (1 2 4 8 16 32 64 128 256)) 0))
    (none-naked)))

(rule "Hidden" "A1:A9" (iferror (+ (* 100 (row)) (match 1 Open!$A1:$I1 0)) (none-naked)))
(rule "Hidden" "A11:I11" (iferror (+ (* 100 (+ 9 (column))) (match 1 Open!A$11:A$19 0)) (none-naked)))
(rule "Hidden" "A21:A29" (iferror (+ (* 100 (- (row) 2)) (match 1 Open!$A21:$I21 0)) (none-naked)))

(defmacro (in-the-unit unit)
  "the variable lies in the unit: a row 1 to 9, a column 10 to 18, a box 19 to 27"
  (priority
    ((<= unit 9) (= (row) unit))
    ((<= unit 18) (= (column) (- unit 9)))
    (else (= (the-box-from 1) (- unit 18)))))

(rule "Forced" "A1:I9"
  (if (and (in-the-unit Ladder!$B$17) (> (bitand Candidates!A83 Ladder!$B$19) 0)) (this-variable) 0))

(defmacro (the-plane-value)
  "the value whose plane this row of Across counts, 1 to 9"
  (+ (int (/ (- (row) 1) 9)) 1))

(defmacro (the-plane-row)
  "the row of variables this row of Across counts, 1 to 9"
  (+ (mod (- (row) 1) 9) 1))

(defmacro (the-band-of line)
  "a row's band or a column's stack, 0 to 2"
  (int (/ (- line 1) 3)))

(defmacro (the-box-places-across)
  "the value's places left in the box this row and stack meet, read from its row of the Boxes"
  (index Boxes!A$1:A$27 (+ (* 3 (- (the-plane-value) 1)) (the-band-of (the-plane-row)) 1)))

(defmacro (a-row-pointing)
  "the box's places for the value, two or more, all on this row, and the row holding more beyond the box"
  (and (>= (the-box-places-across) 2)
       (= A1 (the-box-places-across))
       (> $D1 A1)))

(defmacro (a-row-pointing-key)
  "10000 times the box, 100 times the value, and the row"
  (+ (* 10000 (+ (* 3 (the-band-of (the-plane-row))) (- (column) 4)))
     (* 100 (the-plane-value))
     (the-plane-row)))

(rule "Across" "E1:G81" (if (a-row-pointing) (a-row-pointing-key) (none-pointing)))

(defmacro (the-down-value)
  "the value whose plane this row of Down's pointings counts, 1 to 9, from row 31"
  (+ (int (/ (- (row) 31) 3)) 1))

(defmacro (the-down-band)
  "the band this row of Down's pointings counts, 0 to 2"
  (mod (- (row) 31) 3))

(defmacro (the-box-places-down)
  "the value's places left in the box this band and column meet, read from its row of the Boxes"
  (index Boxes!$A1:$C1 (+ (the-band-of (column)) 1)))

(defmacro (a-column-pointing)
  "the box's places for the value, two or more, all on this column, and the column holding more beyond the box"
  (and (>= (the-box-places-down) 2)
       (= A1 (the-box-places-down))
       (> (index Open!A$11:A$19 (the-down-value)) A1)))

(defmacro (a-column-pointing-key)
  "10000 times the box, 100 times the value, 10 for a column, and the column"
  (+ (* 10000 (+ (* 3 (the-down-band)) (the-band-of (column)) 1))
     (* 100 (the-down-value))
     10
     (column)))

(rule "Down" "A31:I57" (if (a-column-pointing) (a-column-pointing-key) (none-pointing)))

; ---- the Ladder: the next inference, or where it stops (decisions 4, 9 and 10) ----------------
; B1 the kind, 0 none, 1 a naked single, 2 a hidden single, 3 a pointing; B2 its value; B3 the
; place an assignment takes; B4 the value's bit; B5 to B7 a pointing's box, 1 for a column, and
; its line; B9 why there is none, 1 satisfied, 2 a violated constraint, 3 an emptied domain, 4
; a value with no place in a constraint, 5 nothing the three techniques infer. B11 to B22 the
; workings, and B21 the words.
(labels "Ladder" "A1" "kind" "value" "place" "bit" "box" "down" "line" "" "stop")
(labels "Ladder" "A11" "naked" "hidden" "pointing" "violated" "emptied" "no place" "hidden unit" "hidden value" "hidden bit" "hidden place" "words" "unassigned")

(defmacro (a-naked-single) (< Ladder!$B$11 (none-naked)))

(defmacro (a-hidden-single) (< Ladder!$B$12 (none-naked)))

(defmacro (a-pointing) (< Ladder!$B$13 (none-pointing)))

(defmacro (no-place-in units)
  "a unit's values with no place left and none placed, over one of the Open's three tables and its Units"
  (countifs (ref "Open" units) 0 (ref "Units" units) 0))

(rules "Ladder"
  ("B11" (min Naked!A1:I9))
  ("B12" (min Hidden!A1:A9 Hidden!A11:I11 Hidden!A21:A29))
  ("B13" (min Across!E1:G81 Down!A31:I57))
  ("B14" (sum Violations!A1:I9))
  ("B15" (countifs Grid!A1:I9 0 Candidates!A83:I91 0))
  ("B16" (+ (no-place-in "A1:I9") (no-place-in "A11:I19") (no-place-in "A21:I29")))
  ("B17" (int (/ B12 100)))
  ("B18" (mod B12 100))
  ("B19" (if (a-hidden-single) (^ 2 (- B18 1)) 0))
  ("B20" (max Forced!A1:I9))
  ("B22" (- 81 (the-variables-filled)))
  ("B9" (priority
          ((= Lab!$B$11 1) 1)
          ((> B14 0) 2)
          ((> B15 0) 3)
          ((> B16 0) 4)
          ((or (a-naked-single) (a-hidden-single) (a-pointing)) 0)
          (else 5)))
  ("B1" (priority
          ((> B9 0) 0)
          ((a-naked-single) 1)
          ((a-hidden-single) 2)
          (else 3)))
  ("B2" (choose (+ B1 1) 0 (mod B11 10) B18 (mod (int (/ B13 100)) 100)))
  ("B3" (choose (+ B1 1) 0 (int (/ B11 10)) B20 0))
  ("B4" (if (> B2 0) (^ 2 (- B2 1)) 0))
  ("B5" (if (= B1 3) (int (/ B13 10000)) 0))
  ("B6" (if (= B1 3) (mod (int (/ B13 10)) 10) 0))
  ("B7" (if (= B1 3) (mod B13 10) 0)))

; The words (decision 12): a variable by the address the Board's headers show, from B2, and a
; constraint as the variable's row, column or box; a pointing's line by its header, row 6 or
; column F, and its box by the box's first variable.
(defmacro (the-address-of place)
  "a variable's address as the Board's headers show it: E2"
  (address (+ (int (/ (- place 1) 9)) 2) (+ (mod (- place 1) 9) 2) 4))

(defmacro (the-unit-named unit)
  "a unit by its kind, as a variable's constraint: its row, its column or its box"
  (priority
    ((<= unit 9) "row")
    ((<= unit 18) "column")
    (else "box")))

(defmacro (the-line-named)
  "a pointing's line as the Board's headers name it: row 6, or column F"
  (if (= B6 1)
    (& "column " (char (+ 65 B7)))
    (& "row " (+ B7 1))))

(defmacro (the-box-at box)
  "a box by its first variable's address: E5"
  (address (+ (* 3 (int (/ (- box 1) 3))) 2) (+ (* 3 (mod (- box 1) 3)) 2) 4))

(defmacro (counted n one many)
  "n and the words for one or for many"
  (& n " " (if (= n 1) one many)))

(rule "Ladder" "B21"
  (priority
    ((= B9 1) "Satisfied: nothing is left to infer.")
    ((= B9 2) (& "Nothing to infer: " (counted B14 "variable violates" "variables violate") " a constraint."))
    ((= B9 3) (& "Nothing to infer: " (counted B15 "variable has no value left in its domain." "variables have no value left in their domains.")))
    ((= B9 4) (& "Nothing to infer: " (counted B16 "value has" "values have") " no place left in a constraint."))
    ((= B9 5) (& "Nothing the three techniques can infer: " B22 " variables left."))
    ((= B1 1) (& (the-address-of B3) " is " B2 ": the only value left in its domain."))
    ((= B1 2) (& (the-address-of B3) " is " B2 ": the only place left for it in its " (the-unit-named B17) "."))
    (else (& B2 " is struck from the rest of " (the-line-named) ": in the box from " (the-box-at B5) ", every place left for it is on that line."))))

; ---- the marks drawn: all, or filtered (decision 13) ---------------------------------------
; M filters: a mark no longer a candidate is not drawn, kept beneath, and back when a
; retraction widens its domain again.
(rule "Drawn" "A1:I9" (if (= Lab!$B$18 1) (bitand Marks!A1 Candidates!A83) Marks!A1))

; ---- the light: what the Board lights while the ladder is asked (decisions 10 and 11) -------
; A1:I9, each variable's light, laid out as the Grid is: 0 none; 1 a reason, a variable the inference
; is read by; 2 the inference's place, the variable a single assigns or a place a pointing
; strikes its value from; 3 an emptied domain, an unassigned variable with no value left. A
; naked single is read by its assigned neighbors, the variables of its row, its column and
; its box holding a value; a hidden single by its constraint, every variable of it, and every
; variable holding its value; a pointing by its box, every variable of it, and every variable
; holding its value. All of it only while the ladder is asked, so that a wrong digit is not
; flagged before a person asks (CART.14.1's third slice). A11:I19, what an unassigned variable
; shows in its marks' place while it is lit: a single's value at the variable it assigns, before
; the inference is applied, and ∅ at an emptied domain; else nothing, and the marks. The Board
; reads this cell alone, so that a variable whose light keeps its value does not draw its marks
; again at every inference: a cell the language computes again only where what it reads moved.
(defmacro (the-inference-is kind)
  "the inference this frame's ladder names is of the kind: 1 a naked single, 2 a hidden single, 3 a pointing"
  (= Ladder!$B$1 kind))

(defmacro (the-row-of place)
  "a variable's row, 1 to 9, from its place, 1 to 81"
  (+ (int (/ (- place 1) 9)) 1))

(defmacro (the-column-of place)
  "a variable's column, 1 to 9, from its place, 1 to 81"
  (+ (mod (- place 1) 9) 1))

(defmacro (the-box-of place)
  "a variable's box, 1 to 9, from its place, 1 to 81"
  (+ (* 3 (int (/ (- (the-row-of place) 1) 3))) (int (/ (- (the-column-of place) 1) 3)) 1))

(defmacro (beside-the-place)
  "the variable shares a row, a column or a box with the variable the inference assigns"
  (or (= (row) (the-row-of Ladder!$B$3))
      (= (column) (the-column-of Ladder!$B$3))
      (= (the-box-from 1) (the-box-of Ladder!$B$3))))

(defmacro (holding-the-value)
  "the variable holds the value the inference assigns or strikes"
  (= Grid!A1 Ladder!$B$2))

(defmacro (a-place-struck)
  "an unassigned variable the pointing strikes its value from: on its line, outside its box, the value still a candidate"
  (and (= Grid!A1 0)
       (on-the-line-outside-the-box Ladder!$B$6 Ladder!$B$7 Ladder!$B$5)
       (> (bitand Candidates!A83 Ladder!$B$4) 0)))

(defmacro (the-inference-s-place)
  "the variable a single assigns, or a place a pointing strikes its value from"
  (if (the-inference-is 3)
    (a-place-struck)
    (= (this-variable) Ladder!$B$3)))

(defmacro (a-reason)
  "a variable the inference is read by: a naked single's assigned neighbors; a hidden single's constraint and a pointing's box, each whole, and every variable holding the value"
  (priority
    ((the-inference-is 1) (and (> Grid!A1 0) (beside-the-place)))
    ((the-inference-is 2) (or (in-the-unit Ladder!$B$17) (holding-the-value)))
    ((the-inference-is 3) (or (= (the-box-from 1) Ladder!$B$5) (holding-the-value)))
    (else false)))

(defmacro (an-emptied-domain)
  "an unassigned variable with no value left in its domain"
  (and (= Grid!A1 0) (= Candidates!A83 0)))

(rule "Light" "A1:I9"
  (priority
    ((= Lab!$B$13 0) 0)                        ; the ladder not asked: nothing lit
    ((an-emptied-domain) 3)
    ((the-inference-s-place) 2)
    ((a-reason) 1)
    (else 0)))

(defmacro (the-empty-domain)
  "what an emptied domain shows while the light names it: the empty set, U+2205"
  "∅")

(defmacro (a-single-s-place)
  "the light names this variable as the place a single assigns: a naked or a hidden single's, not a pointing's"
  (and (= A1 2) (< Ladder!$B$1 3)))

(rule "Light" "A11:I19"
  (priority
    ((a-single-s-place) Ladder!$B$2)            ; the single's value, before it is applied
    ((= A1 3) (the-empty-domain))
    (else "")))

; ---- the Board: what a person sees -------------------------------------------------------
; An assigned variable shows its value, and so, while the light names it, does the variable a
; single assigns, before the inference is applied; an emptied domain the light names shows
; ∅. Each draws through a look, and the rules over the Board say its state (CART.14.1's
; third slice, where a code a value stood: 100 times its kind, 10 times its box's parity and
; the value). An unassigned variable shows its marks drawn, all of them or, filtered, those
; still candidates: a digit or a figure space in each of nine places, three figure spaces
; between two of a line, and two line feeds between two lines, which its own format draws as
; five lines, centered, three of marks and an empty line between two of them, so that each
; mark stands centered in its third of the cell; or nothing. A figure space is no workaround
; for a family: a wrapped line's trailing spaces hang and move nothing, in Excel's drawing and
; the page's, so a line whose last mark is not there would stand centered by its first.
; The Board stands from B2, a margin row and column before it in the canvas's gray, so that its
; frame's top and left draw as its right and bottom do: Excel draws no line of a cell's on
; row 1's top or column A's left, beside the headers, and the page draws as Excel does (the
; owner's hand test, 2026-10-29).
(defmacro (figure-space)
  "where a mark is not: a digit's width of nothing, U+2007"
  " ")

(defmacro (between-marks)
  "three figure spaces between two marks of a line, so that each stands centered in its third of the cell"
  "   ")

(defmacro (between-lines)
  "two line feeds, a line of marks ended and an empty line between it and the next, so that each mark stands in its third of the cell (ENGINE.36)"
  (& (char 10) (char 10)))

(defmacro (a-mark bit digit)
  "the digit where the marks drawn hold its bit, else a figure space"
  (if (= (bit-of Drawn!A1 bit) 1) digit (figure-space)))

(defmacro (the-marks)
  "an unassigned variable's marks as text, three lines of three, each digit in its place"
  (&
    (a-mark 1 "1") (between-marks) (a-mark 2 "2") (between-marks) (a-mark 4 "3") (between-lines)
    (a-mark 8 "4") (between-marks) (a-mark 16 "5") (between-marks) (a-mark 32 "6") (between-lines)
    (a-mark 64 "7") (between-marks) (a-mark 128 "8") (between-marks) (a-mark 256 "9")))

(rule "Board" "B2:J10"
  (priority
    ((> Grid!A1 0) Grid!A1)
    ((<> Light!A11 "") Light!A11)               ; a single's value, or an emptied domain's ∅, while lit
    ((= Drawn!A1 0) "")
    (else (the-marks))))

; The ladder's words on the row under the Board, while infer or propagate has lit them and no
; other command has put them out, on the gray over the empty cells to the right (decision 12).
(rule "Board" "B11" (if (= Lab!$B$13 1) Ladder!$B$21 ""))

; Each variable's own format, one of nine by its place in its box (ENGINE.28): its edges
; medium where the place lies on its box's bound and thin within, so that the lines tell the
; boxes, as tints told them until then; its marks wrapped and centered both ways, their five
; lines in the cell's middle; and no fill. A place counts from 1 at its box's top left to 9 at
; its bottom right, a column and a row of the box, each 0 to 2; a style row names one cell,
; since no place is a rectangle.
(defmacro (box-line at bound)
  "a side's line: medium where the place lies on its box's bound, thin within"
  (quote-if (=expand at bound) medium thin))

(defmacro (place-format p column row)
  "the place p's format, at the column and the row of its box: its four edges, its marks centered"
  (format p none general wrap (align center middle)
    (border
      (left (box-line column 0))
      (right (box-line column 2))
      (top (box-line row 0))
      (bottom (box-line row 2)))))

(place-format 1 0 0) (place-format 2 1 0) (place-format 3 2 0)   ; the box's top row, its top edges medium
(place-format 4 0 1) (place-format 5 1 1) (place-format 6 2 1)   ; its middle row, thin above and below
(place-format 7 0 2) (place-format 8 1 2) (place-format 9 2 2)   ; its bottom row, its bottom edges medium

(defmacro (place-at r c)
  "the place of the variable at the row r and the column c: three a row down its box, one a column across"
  (+expand 1 (+expand (*expand 3 (mod-expand (-expand r 1) 3)) (mod-expand (-expand c 1) 3))))

(each (r (1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9))
  (each (c (1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9))
    (style "Board" (address-expand (+expand r 1) (+expand c 1)) (place-at r c))))

; A variable 12.57 characters wide and 66 points tall, 88 pixels square, twice the size it
; first had (the owner's hand test, 2026-10-19): a line of marks, nine digits wide, fits it,
; and a line, a space and four figure spaces do not, so the marks wrap into five lines, the
; first, third and fifth of them marks, in their places. The columns from B and the rows from
; 2; every column's empty cells in the canvas's gray, the margin's among them.
(widths "Board" 2 10 12.57 111)
(heights "Board" 2 10 66)

(on "Board" (column "A" 1.71 shown 111) (row 1 9 shown))   ; the margin, 12 pixels each way

; ---- the look: Lovelace Lavender, by rules ---------------------------------------------------
; A variable holds its own digit (CART.14.1's third slice), and its look draws it bold at 22
; points, twice the marks' size; ∅ the same. A look says no alignment and no edge, so the
; cell's own format centers the digit and draws its box's lines. Then six rules over the Board
; lay what the variable's state says over what it draws (KERNEL.58, drawn since ENGINE.37),
; the first winning what it says and the later lending what it leaves: the satisfied board
; Lovelace Lavender itself and its lighter shade, by box, every digit white, stopping the rest
; (the owner's hand test, 2026-10-29); the inference's place in Lovelace Lavender, white
; (decision 11); a violation, and an emptied domain while the ladder is asked, on
; Superposition's red (decision 10); a reason on the pale lavender; and an assignment's digit
; in the family's deep lavender, a given's in the host's ink. A rule says no size and no
; family, which a conditional format in Excel never sets; the look says the size.
(format 10 (font bold 22))                    ; a value's digit, and the emptied domain: bold at 22 points
(format 11 (fill "A080E0") (font "FFFFFF"))   ; Lovelace Lavender, white: the satisfied board's boxes 1, 3, 5, 7 and 9, and the inference's place
(format 12 (fill "B9A3E7") (font "FFFFFF"))   ; its lighter shade, white: the satisfied board's other boxes
(format 13 (fill "FFD5D5"))                   ; Superposition's red: a violation, and an emptied domain
(format 14 (fill "E6DFF7"))                   ; the pale lavender: a reason
(format 15 (font "6B4FC8"))                   ; the family's deep lavender: an assignment's digit

(each (v (1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9))
  (look "Board" v 10))

(look "Board" (the-empty-domain) 10)

(defmacro (the-odd-boxes)
  "the boxes 1, 3, 5, 7 and 9, Lovelace Lavender itself on the satisfied board"
  "B2:D4 H2:J4 E5:G7 B8:D10 H8:J10")

(defmacro (the-even-boxes)
  "the boxes 2, 4, 6 and 8, its lighter shade"
  "E2:G4 B5:D7 H5:J7 E8:G10")

(defmacro (a-light priority range test laid)
  "a rule over the Board: its priority, the cells it answers for, its test an expression, and the format it lays"
  (conditional "Board" priority range (formula-expand test) laid))

(defmacro (a-last-light priority range test laid)
  "a rule over the Board that stops every later rule at a cell it lights"
  (conditional "Board" priority range (formula-expand test) laid stop))

(a-last-light 1 (the-odd-boxes) (= Lab!$B$11 1) 11)                       ; satisfied
(a-last-light 2 (the-even-boxes) (= Lab!$B$11 1) 12)                      ; satisfied
(a-light 3 "B2:J10" (= Light!A1 2) 11)                                    ; the inference's place
(a-light 4 "B2:J10" (or (= Violations!A1 1) (= Light!A1 3)) 13)           ; violated, or emptied
(a-light 5 "B2:J10" (= Light!A1 1) 14)                                    ; a reason
(a-light 6 "B2:J10" (and (> Grid!A1 0) (= Givens!A1 0)) 15)               ; an assignment
(on "Board" (gridlines off))                            ; the edges draw every line of the Board

; ---- the keys, beside the Board (the owner's hand test, 2026-10-19) ---------------------------
; What each key does, a key a row beside the variables: L the key, M its words, both on the
; canvas's gray, the headers' own, which a bound sheet stands on, so that the Board alone is
; white; K a gutter of the same gray; the keys bold and centered in their column (the owner's
; hand test, 2026-10-29). The marks' keys drawn as the marks are, in five lines, each key in
; its mark's place (the owner's second look, 2026-10-29): three letters a line, three spaces
; between two of them and two line feeds between two lines, in a family whose letters and
; spaces are one width, Consolas, or the platform's monospace where it has none (ENGINE.37),
; so that each stands in its third as a digit does. Its lines end in a letter, so no space
; hangs, and the fullwidth letters that stood there until CART.14.1's third slice are gone.
(format 111 "F3F3EE" general nowrap)   ; a key's words
(format 112 "F3F3EE" general wrap (font bold (family "Consolas" mono)) (align center middle))   ; the marks' keys, in their places and centered as the marks are, one width a letter
(format 113 "F3F3EE" general nowrap (font bold) (align center middle))   ; a key, bold and centered in its column
(cells "Board"
  ("L2" "1 to 9") ("M2" "assign the value to the variable, row or keypad")
  ("L3" "Backspace") ("M3" "retract the assignment, or strike the marks")
  ("M4" "mark a value in the domain, at its key's place")
  ("L5" "F") ("M5" "fill every domain with what its constraints allow")
  ("L6" "R") ("M6" "retract every assignment and every mark")
  ("L7" "N") ("M7" "deal a new instance")
  ("L8" "G") ("M8" "the next instance's grade, 1 to 4 and round")
  ("L9" "I") ("M9" "say the next inference, and again to apply it")
  ("L10" "P") ("M10" "propagate to the fixed point, and say where it stopped")
  ("L11" "U") ("M11" "retract what inference assigned")
  ("L12" "M") ("M12" "draw only the marks the constraints allow, or all")
  ("L13" "← ↑ → ↓") ("M13" "move the selection, as a click does")
  ("L14" "Ctrl+K") ("M14" "every command, by its name"))
(rule "Board" "L4"
  (& "Q   W   E" (between-lines) "A   S   D" (between-lines) "Z   X   C"))

(on "Board"
  (style "L2:L3" 113)                ; the first two keys
  (style "L4" 112)                   ; the marks' keys
  (style "L5:L14" 113)               ; the rest of the keys
  (style "M2:M14" 111)               ; their words
  (style "B11" 111))                 ; the ladder's words, on the gray as the keys' words are, lit or not
; the gutter's empty cells by its column's format; the keys' column a variable's width, so that
; the marks' keys lie as the marks do; the words' column as wide as the longest words
(on "Board" (column "K" 3 shown 111) (column "L" 12.57 shown 111) (column "M" 48 shown 111))

; ---- the Constraints: the counts, and each constraint's state -----------------------------
(cells "Constraints"
  ("A1" "Seiyaku 制約")
  ("A2" "Eighty-one variables, twenty-seven constraints, one solution, proven before you began."))
(labels "Constraints" "A4" "instance" "grade" "puzzle in the book" "seed" "next instance's grade")

(defmacro (grade-named grade)
  "a grade's name: the hardest technique its puzzles need"
  (choose grade "naked singles" "hidden singles" "pointing pairs" "beyond the three"))

(rules "Constraints"
  ("B4" (+ Lab!B2 1))
  ("B5" Lab!B5)
  ("C5" (grade-named Lab!B5))
  ("B6" Deal!B1)
  ("B7" Clock!B3)
  ("B8" Lab!B4)
  ("C8" (grade-named Lab!B4)))
; The counts: the assignments the person's and inference's, inference's counted apart, so
; that "satisfied, in 3 acts" says how (CART.14.1, decision 12); and the next inference, the
; Board's words, while they are lit.
(labels "Constraints" "A10" "givens" "assignments" "inferred" "unassigned" "violated variables" "violated constraints" "marks kept" "acts" "next inference" "satisfied")
(rules "Constraints"
  ("B10" (countif Givens!A1:I9 ">0"))
  ("B11" (- (the-variables-filled) B10))
  ("B12" (sum Inferred!A1:I9))
  ("B13" (- 81 (the-variables-filled)))
  ("B14" (sum Violations!A1:I9))
  ("B15" (sum D34:D60))
  ("B16" (sum Marks!A11:I19))
  ("B17" Lab!B1)
  ("B18" (if (= Lab!B13 1) Ladder!B21 ""))
  ("B19" (if (= Lab!B11 1) (& "satisfied, in " Lab!B12 " acts") "not yet"))
  ("B20" (if (= Lab!B11 1) "No search was performed by the cartridge." "")))

; Each value's count on the board, 9 of each when satisfied, a value a row.
(headers "Constraints" "A22" "value" "placed")
(labels "Constraints" "A23" 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9)

(rule "Constraints" "B23:B31" (countif Grid!$A$1:$I$9 A23))

; The twenty-seven constraints: each its variables assigned and its state, violated where a
; value counts twice, satisfied where nine are assigned and none is violated, open else.
(headers "Constraints" "A33" "constraint" "assigned" "state" "violated")
(labels "Constraints" "A34"
  "row 1" "row 2" "row 3" "row 4" "row 5" "row 6" "row 7" "row 8" "row 9"
  "column 1" "column 2" "column 3" "column 4" "column 5" "column 6" "column 7" "column 8" "column 9"
  "box 1" "box 2" "box 3" "box 4" "box 5" "box 6" "box 7" "box 8" "box 9")

(defmacro (state-of counts assigned)
  "a constraint's state from its counts and its variables assigned: violated where a value counts twice, satisfied where nine are assigned and none is violated, open else"
  (if (> (max counts) 1) "violated" (if (= assigned 9) "satisfied" "open")))

(rules "Constraints"
  ("B34:B42" (sum Units!$A1:$I1))
  ("C34:C42" (state-of Units!$A1:$I1 B34))
  ("B52:B60" (sum Units!$A21:$I21))
  ("C52:C60" (state-of Units!$A21:$I21 B52))
  ("D34:D60" (if (= C34 "violated") 1 0)))

(defmacro (a-column-of-the-units c)
  "the column c's counts, down the Units' rows 11 to 19"
  (ref "Units" (&expand (column-letters-expand c) "11:" (column-letters-expand c) "19")))

(each (c (1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9))                          ; the column c's constraint, on the row 42 + c
  (rule "Constraints" (address-expand (+expand 42 c) 2)
    (sum (a-column-of-the-units c)))
  (rule "Constraints" (address-expand (+expand 42 c) 3)
    (state-of (a-column-of-the-units c) (symbol "B" (+expand 42 c)))))

; Column B twelve characters wide, so that a seed of ten digits, which a person reads off to share an instance, reads
; whole (Superposition's catch at CART.12's hand test).
(on "Constraints" (column "A" 22 shown none) (column "B" 12 shown none) (column "C" 18 shown none))

; ---- the book ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; A puzzle a row of the hidden Book, its 81 values from A to CC, a dot no cell, written by
; the kit's picture with its hex legend. The book is ordered by grade, 32 a grade, so a
; puzzle's grade is the block it stands in.
; ---- the book, written by cargo run --release --example seiyaku: edit the generator, never these lines ----
(picture "Book" "A1" hex
